# Build context: the module root (the last argument of `docker build`).
#
# Docker only reads .dockerignore from the root of the build context, not from
# the directory holding the Dockerfile, so this file has to stay here.
#
# Only the source tree and the vendor package archives are needed; the rest of
# the repository (git metadata, Go caches, macOS artefacts) would just slow the
# context upload down.
#
# docker/packages is deliberately NOT excluded: the Dockerfiles copy the
# CryptoPro archives from it with `COPY ${CRYPTOPRO_PKG} ...`.

.git
**/.gocache
**/.gopath
**/.verify-cache
**/.DS_Store
